ntp.ntpc: load libntpc by its runtime soname (libntpc.so.1).

The Python library looked for libntpc.so only -- the unversioned
development symlink, which the QNX packages (like any distribution's) ship
in ntpsec-dev. With just ntpsec installed every ntp.* module failed to import
("Can't find ntpc library"), and with it ntpdig, ntpq, ntpkeygen and the
other Python clients. Try libntpc.so.1 first in each place searched.

Upstream-Status: QNX-specific

--- a/pylib/ntpc.py
+++ b/pylib/ntpc.py
@@ -40,6 +40,12 @@ def _importado():
         "@LIBDIR@" + os.sep + library_basename,
     ]
 
+    # The unversioned libntpc.so is a development symlink, which packagers
+    # (QNX's included) ship in the -dev package: try the runtime soname,
+    # libntpc.so.1, first in each place.
+    ntpc_paths = [v for p in ntpc_paths
+                  for v in ((p + ".1", p) if p.endswith(".so") else (p,))]
+
     # Finally, check in ordinary library folders for production use.
     ntpc_path = ctypes.util.find_library(LIB)
     if ntpc_path:
